    "created_at": "2017-02-14T19:52:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-14T19:52:12Z",
    "body": "I'll need to test in implementations. The PR I just put up differs from Blink implementation in that it only looks at the flag after the dispatch is complete, whereas Blink aborts the transaction after the first callback that throws (so which would be in the \"inner invoke\" steps). In other words, throwing in the first listener would change state before the event made it to the second listener. \r\n\r\n(I suspect changing that would be web-compatible, but need tests anyway.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
